            "overlay_texts": [
                "Taro&#039;s palms press against the bark of a three-hundred-year-old sentinel, and for the first time in seven years, he feels the Slow One&#039;s acknowledgmentnot as a surge or a song, but as a readjustment in the wood grain itself, a patient tightening of rings that were always growing. Young man 23 years old with a lean athletic build and calm detached presence, rendered in refined anime style with sharp youthful facial proportions, narrow jaw, small straight nose, slightly downturned serious pale blue-white eyes. His tousled medium-length white-blueish hair with layered spiky strands catches subtle highlights as he leans into the ancient tree. The short cropped red leather jacket with high open collar and fat white outlines bears visible stitch lines, reinforced shoulder panels with horizontal quilting, exposed brushed steel zipper, and a small stitched geometric emblem patch on the left shoulder. Underneath, a lightweight gray crew shirt of fine-knit modal-cotton texture shows realistic fabric folds at the neckline. A geometric diamond-shaped matte silver pendant with etched pattern hangs centered at his chest on an almost-invisible chain. Black fingerless gloves with knuckle seam reinforcement and visible scuffing grip the tree bark. His slim dark charcoal tactical pants feature articulated knee seams and reflective piping along outer thigh seams, cinched with a low-profile utility belt with brushed hex-buckle. Black boots with reinforced toe caps and lug soles complete the lived-in ensemble. His breath steadies as the Vitalis glow rises from his fingertips in a dreamy, unsatisfied tempo. Around him the Shadow-Scab&#039;s canopy shifts in unison, a nonstop whisper of leaves like the jungle chronicling who finally learned to listen. The cost settles into his marrow as sap beads at the contact pointspersimmon-gold, the color of something that has learned the discipline of roots. A worshipper&#039;s relief crosses his face as the partnership becomes irrevocable, written in heartwood and enduring assiduity. The moment suspends between connection and sacrifice, the ancient tree and the young man locked in a covenant older than words."
            ],
